The full command is the positive proof suite and closes both
SPEC.loop-invariant and SPEC.f-correct together. A diagnostic command selecting
only SPEC.f-correct exits 1 at the first loop iteration because selection also
removes the auxiliary loop circularity. Its residual is
  vCons(1,.ValSeq) = resultRun(.ValSeq,1,N,1,0)
under 1 <= N and not 2 <= N. This is expected dependency evidence, not a
failure of the full two-claim reachability proof.
